# Phaneroo SACCO transactional alerts behind Caddy.
#
# LIVE HOST: /alerts/* on sacco.pivotventures.tech is proxied to
# 127.0.0.1:8095 by a route that was added through the Caddy admin API
# (localhost:2019). The on-disk /etc/caddy/Caddyfile on that host is
# incomplete. Do not `caddy reload`, `caddy adapt --config
# /etc/caddy/Caddyfile`, or replace the running config with that file.
# A reload would drop /alerts/* and any other admin-API route that is not
# in the file. Deploy SACCO Alerts does not call the admin API and does
# not reload Caddy, nginx, Fineract, or the payments gateway.
#
# The process accepts both /alerts/api/v1/... (what the live proxy sends)
# and /v1/... (what handle_path below would send). Do not change the live
# proxy to apply this snippet until the host Caddyfile is complete.
#
# This snippet is not part of deploy/production/caddy/routes.caddy. That
# file is the gateway container allowlist for Desk paths
# (/transactional-alerts/*, /payments-portal/*). Inside the container,
# 127.0.0.1 is not this process.
#
# Production Desk is served by Caddy (see desk/README.md). If you paste
# this inside a complete site block, put it next to the /payments and
# /fineract-provider reverse_proxy lines. Do not replace those lines or
# the desk file_server. Run `caddy validate` before any reload.
#
# Auth is done by the alerts service itself:
#   - Desk staff send X-Staff-Authorization: Basic <desk key>; the service
#     verifies it against Fineract. Caddy passes it through untouched.
#   - The member gateway sends X-Alerts-Service-Key, but it talks to
#     127.0.0.1:8095 (or the backend network) directly, never through
#     Caddy. Caddy therefore strips any client-supplied copy.
# Caddy never injects a key. Do not add one here.
#
# Rate limiting: stock Caddy has no rate limiter. If this host fronts the
# public internet, use the nginx snippet (limit_req) or a Caddy build with
# the caddy-ratelimit module.

# handle_path strips the /alerts/api prefix:
# /alerts/api/v1/health -> http://127.0.0.1:8095/v1/health
handle_path /alerts/api/* {
	request_body {
		max_size 64KB
	}
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8095 {
		# Strip internal-only credentials a client may try to forge.
		header_up -X-Alerts-Service-Key
		header_up -X-Alerts-Key
		transport http {
			dial_timeout 5s
			response_header_timeout 30s
			read_timeout 30s
			write_timeout 15s
		}
	}
}
